&lt;i&gt;Ah, summer's here again&lt;/i&gt;

11
00:00:41,195 --> 00:00:43,906
&lt;i&gt;It's come, it's arrived, it's here&lt;/i&gt;

12
00:00:44,115 --> 00:00:46,909
&lt;i&gt;Ah, summer's here again&lt;/i&gt;

13
00:00:47,118 --> 00:00:49,412
&lt;i&gt;It's come, it's arrived,&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;it's here already!&lt;/i&gt;

14
00:00:49,620 --> 00:00:52,623
&lt;i&gt;Big waves, small waves,&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;tiny waves and middle-size waves&lt;/i&gt;

15
00:00:52,832 --> 00:00:55,460
&lt;i&gt;Here they come on the southern wind&lt;/i&gt;

16
00:00:55,668 --> 00:00:58,463
&lt;i&gt;Big butts, small butts,&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;tiny butts and middle-size butts&lt;/i&gt;

17
00:00:58,671 --> 00:01:02,967
&lt;i&gt;At the beach&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;Jiggle, jiggle, jiggle&lt;/i&gt;

18
00:01:06,137 --> 00:01:15,480
&lt;i&gt;Here they come on the southern wind&lt;/i&gt;

19
00:01:17,982 --> 00:01:22,028
&lt;i&gt;Bouncing at the beach&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;Jiggling at the beach&lt;/i&gt;

20
00:01:23,279 --> 00:01:24,363
&lt;i&gt;Want you!&lt;/i&gt;

21
00:01:28,242 --> 00:01:34,207
A ROOKIE COP FROM THE HEAVENS

22
00:01:35,750 --> 00:01:37,835
What nice weather.

23
00:01:38,211 --> 00:01:41,047
Today's going to be a good day...

24
00:01:42,757 --> 00:01:45,593
Wait. It's too quiet.

25
00:01:46,052 --> 00:01:48,262
That can only mean...

26
00:01:49,347 --> 00:01:51,349
Ryotsu must be late again!

27
00:01:51,933 --> 00:01:53,392
Nope.

28
00:01:54,769 --> 00:01:55,561
Hmm?

29
00:01:59,065 --> 00:02:02,360
What? Ryotsu is working?!

30
00:02:02,568 --> 00:02:06,239
He came in two hours early and has been hard at work ever since.

31
00:02:06,447 --> 00:02:09,617
We were just saying it must be some kind of omen.

32
00:02:09,992 --> 00:02:10,785
Eh?

33
00:02:10,993 --> 00:02:14,664
This is incredible.

34
00:02:14,872 --> 00:02:17,625
In my 30 years as a police officer,

35
00:02:17,833 --> 00:02:20,253
I've never been happier!

36
00:02:20,711 --> 00:02:21,712
Here you are, Chief.

37
00:02:23,005 --> 00:02:24,841
But is it that incredible?

38
00:02:25,049 --> 00:02:28,427
Yes. Ryotsu has finally started taking his work seriously.

39
00:02:28,636 --> 00:02:31,222
All my efforts have paid off.

40
00:02:31,597 --> 00:02:33,683
All right! I'm done!

41
00:02:34,183 --> 00:02:37,979
Well done, Ryotsu! I knew you'd turn over a new leaf eventually.

42
00:02:38,187 --> 00:02:40,648
By the way, what forms were you writing?

43
00:02:40,856 --> 00:02:44,068
What? Did you forget, Chief?

44
00:02:44,277 --> 00:02:48,781
These are the written apologies you ordered me to submit yesterday.

45
00:02:49,156 --> 00:02:50,867
W-Written apologies?

46
00:02:51,492 --> 00:02:53,953
I finished all of them.

47
00:02:54,161 --> 00:02:56,581
Huh? What happened to the massage...?

48
00:02:56,998 --> 00:02:59,750
You idiot!

49
00:03:04,589 --> 00:03:06,841
You blockhead!

50
00:03:08,217 --> 00:03:10,636
Chief! Are you okay?

51
00:03:11,429 --> 00:03:14,098
-Sorry. Get me my pills... -Of course.

52
00:03:15,766 --> 00:03:17,476
You're taking too many, Chief.

53
00:03:17,685 --> 00:03:21,314
You should be careful with those at your age.

54
00:03:21,522 --> 00:03:22,440
What did you say?!

55
00:03:22,648 --> 00:03:24,817
It's your fault that I need them!

56
00:03:25,026 --> 00:03:26,652
Chief, please calm down.

57
00:03:26,861 --> 00:03:29,322
You'll burst a blood vessel.

58
00:03:33,159 --> 00:03:38,247
I give up. I guess I'll just have to put up with this useless idiot.

59
00:03:39,081 --> 00:03:43,002
Anyway, never mind him, has Nakagawa arrived yet?

60
00:03:43,210 --> 00:03:44,503
Nakagawa-san?

61
00:03:44,712 --> 00:03:47,798
He's supposed to be joining our team from today.

62
00:03:48,007 --> 00:03:49,258
What's he like?

63
00:03:50,051 --> 00:03:52,136
Wow. He's quite a handsome guy.

64
00:03:52,595 --> 00:03:55,431
He lived in New York until he was 16.

65
00:03:55,640 --> 00:03:58,100
So he grew up overseas, just like you, Reiko-san.

66
00:03:58,309 --> 00:03:59,101
Yeah.

67
00:03:59,769 --> 00:04:04,357
He has an advanced driving license, and can sail boats and fly planes as well.

68
00:04:04,565 --> 00:04:07,652
He's a great sportsman and speaks foreign languages too.

69
00:04:07,860 --> 00:04:11,614
And he can shoot the head off a needle from a kilometer away.

70
00:04:12,031 --> 00:04:14,367
He sounds amazing.

71
00:04:14,825 --> 00:04:16,869
He's the heir to the Nakagawa Corporation.

72
00:04:17,244 --> 00:04:19,288
The Nakagawa Corporation?!

73
00:04:19,497 --> 00:04:23,292
That's one of the biggest companies in the world.

74
00:04:23,501 --> 00:04:24,293
That's right.

75
00:04:24,835 --> 00:04:28,506
What's this Nakagawa thing you're talking about?

76
00:04:29,048 --> 00:04:32,718
It's a corporation. A big company.

77
00:04:32,927 --> 00:04:34,178
Oh, no big deal then.

78
00:04:34,387 --> 00:04:36,681
Huh? Were you listening?

79
00:04:36,889 --> 00:04:39,517
Reiko, don't waste your time on this fool.

80
00:04:39,725 --> 00:04:41,977
You'll end up with stomach problems like me.

81
00:04:42,561 --> 00:04:43,354
Okay, Chief.

82
00:04:43,771 --> 00:04:48,776
There's no way some spoiled rich kid can make a decent cop.

83
00:04:48,984 --> 00:04:51,487
He'll give up straight away and run off.

84
00:04:51,696 --> 00:04:56,784
If that's what you think, I'm making you responsible for training him!

85
00:04:56,993 --> 00:04:57,868
What?

86
00:05:04,458 --> 00:05:06,293
Now's my chance.

87
00:05:13,426 --> 00:05:15,261
Pretty awesome, huh?

88
00:05:16,220 --> 00:05:19,598
It's a combat rescue helicopter used by the US military.

89
00:05:19,807 --> 00:05:20,891
You're unbelievable.

90
00:05:21,100 --> 00:05:23,936
You skipped work yesterday to make this, didn't you?

91
00:05:24,395 --> 00:05:25,187
Well, yeah.

92
00:05:25,688 --> 00:05:28,691
The chief'll definitely burst something if he hears about this.

93
00:05:30,151 --> 00:05:31,360
Now then...

94
00:05:34,572 --> 00:05:36,073
That's odd...

95
00:05:36,282 --> 00:05:37,950
Where's the remote control?

96
00:05:38,159 --> 00:05:40,369
Why is your locker in such a state?

97
00:05:40,578 --> 00:05:42,621
Ah! I remember!

98
00:05:45,583 --> 00:05:48,377
When did you make that secret compartment?

99
00:05:48,586 --> 00:05:50,921
Oh, you didn't know about it?

100
00:05:51,505 --> 00:05:54,091
This is supposed to be a police station...

101
00:05:58,929 --> 00:06:01,307
Easy does it...

102
00:06:04,226 --> 00:06:06,103
Ready to fly?

103
00:06:07,313 --> 00:06:09,315
Good boy!

104
00:06:09,982 --> 00:06:12,610
This contraption is quite well made.

105
00:06:12,818 --> 00:06:16,739
If only he took his police work this seriously.

106
00:06:17,698 --> 00:06:19,200
I always work hard.

107
00:06:21,619 --> 00:06:22,870
Sorry about that!

108
00:06:23,412 --> 00:06:24,997
Ryo-chan!

109
00:06:29,460 --> 00:06:30,753
Ryo-san?

110
00:06:34,298 --> 00:06:36,008
What's all this noise?

111
00:06:36,592 --> 00:06:38,969
Are you okay?

112
00:06:40,596 --> 00:06:42,264
I thought I was done for.

113
00:06:42,473 --> 00:06:43,974
Where's the helicopter?

114
00:06:44,934 --> 00:06:45,768
Helicopter?

115
00:06:45,976 --> 00:06:46,977
It flew away.

116
00:06:47,186 --> 00:06:50,147
Argh! That cost me 30,000 yen!

117
00:06:50,898 --> 00:06:52,775
If I need a replacement, you're paying!

118
00:06:52,983 --> 00:06:56,403
No way! You're the one in the wrong.

119
00:06:56,904 --> 00:06:59,865
Damn! Where did it fly off to?

120
00:07:01,575 --> 00:07:03,702
Hey, another helicopter.

121
00:07:03,911 --> 00:07:05,913
It brought a friend back with it.

122
00:07:12,086 --> 00:07:14,672
Why you! How dare you destroy my helicopter!

123
00:07:14,880 --> 00:07:16,006
What's going on?

124
00:07:16,215 --> 00:07:18,008
A helicopter's coming our way!

125
00:07:18,342 --> 00:07:19,135
What?

126
00:07:22,054 --> 00:07:23,013
What's that?

127
00:07:23,222 --> 00:07:25,474
Who the heck is it?

128
00:07:40,990 --> 00:07:42,741
He's got a bazooka!

129
00:07:50,082 --> 00:07:51,625
Yahoo!

130
00:08:02,636 --> 00:08:05,222
Sorry I'm late, everyone.

131
00:08:05,431 --> 00:08:08,267
Officer Keiichi Nakagawa reporting for duty.

132
00:08:08,475 --> 00:08:11,312
I look forward to working with you.

133
00:08:11,520 --> 00:08:15,399
You jerk! You destroyed my helicopter!

134
00:08:15,608 --> 00:08:19,069
That's a Walther MPL submachine gun!

135
00:08:19,570 --> 00:08:22,323
You recognize it? I'm glad.

136
00:08:22,531 --> 00:08:24,074
I've got this pistol too.

137
00:08:24,450 --> 00:08:27,745
Whoa, it's the same gun that Dirty Harry uses!

138
00:08:28,495 --> 00:08:30,623
That was a great movie, wasn't it?

139
00:08:31,415 --> 00:08:34,460
Perhaps you'd accept it as compensation for your helicopter?

140
00:08:34,668 --> 00:08:36,795
You serious? I'll take it!

141
00:08:37,004 --> 00:08:40,257
It's fine, really. I have plenty more at home.

142
00:08:40,466 --> 00:08:41,425
You should come sometime.

143
00:08:41,634 --> 00:08:43,052
I will!

144
00:08:43,260 --> 00:08:45,554
You idiot!

145
00:08:46,597 --> 00:08:49,141
What in the world are you thinking?

146
00:08:49,350 --> 00:08:51,268
I'm confiscating those!

147
00:08:51,810 --> 00:08:54,146
Is this not allowed either?

148
00:08:54,980 --> 00:08:57,024
Of course not...

149
00:08:57,942 --> 00:09:00,319
Terai, you confiscate the rest.

150
00:09:00,527 --> 00:09:01,737
Yes, Chief!

151
00:09:03,572 --> 00:09:06,408
My stomach is playing up again...

152
00:09:06,617 --> 00:09:10,037
Reiko, please take over for today. I'm going to the doctor.

153
00:09:11,288 --> 00:09:14,041
There's a lot to like about you.

154
00:09:14,249 --> 00:09:16,043
I'm Ryotsu! Nice to meet you!

155
00:09:16,752 --> 00:09:20,798
Oh, you're Ryotsu-san? I've heard so much about you!

156
00:09:21,131 --> 00:09:23,467
It's very nice to meet you.

157
00:09:24,259 --> 00:09:26,637
I guess we've got two naughty kids now.

158
00:09:26,845 --> 00:09:29,682
You don't seem too upset about it...

159
00:09:32,851 --> 00:09:35,020
That helicopter was your own, huh?

160
00:09:36,480 --> 00:09:38,732
I thought you weren't a big deal.

161
00:09:39,775 --> 00:09:41,026
A big deal?

162
00:09:42,236 --> 00:09:44,989
Never mind. What made you want to be a police officer?

163
00:09:46,448 --> 00:09:47,658
Well, you see...

164
00:09:48,617 --> 00:09:51,287
When I lived in New York, there was a lot of crime.

165
00:09:51,495 --> 00:09:54,415
I always looked up to the police officers

166
00:09:54,623 --> 00:09:56,959
who risked their lives to protect the public.

167
00:09:59,670 --> 00:10:04,717
So, what's with the flashy uniform?

168
00:10:04,925 --> 00:10:05,801
Huh?

169
00:10:06,010 --> 00:10:09,013
Yeah. That seems like more of a problem than the guns.

170
00:10:09,221 --> 00:10:10,472
Is it?

171
00:10:10,681 --> 00:10:13,726
The Japanese police uniform isn't very stylish.

172
00:10:13,934 --> 00:10:16,103
So I had one tailor-made for me by Armani.

173
00:10:17,604 --> 00:10:19,023
It cost about a million yen.

174
00:10:20,858 --> 00:10:22,609
A million yen?!

175
00:10:23,902 --> 00:10:26,739
You could have just worn a normal one for free!

176
00:10:27,364 --> 00:10:30,993
Look who's talking. You spent 30,000 yen on an RC helicopter.

177
00:10:31,201 --> 00:10:32,202
That's different.

178
00:10:32,411 --> 00:10:33,454
Sure it is.

179
00:10:33,662 --> 00:10:39,001
Anyway, the higher-ups at HQ must have softened up if they let you wear that.

180
00:10:39,585 --> 00:10:43,756
Actually, they said I couldn't. But I changed clothes in the helicopter.

181
00:10:44,381 --> 00:10:46,008
That's dedication!

182
00:10:49,219 --> 00:10:51,722
I understand how the chief feels...

183
00:10:51,930 --> 00:10:53,640
I'm going out on patrol.

184
00:10:53,849 --> 00:10:56,852
Ryo-chan, make sure you show Nakagawa-san the ropes.

185
00:10:57,269 --> 00:10:58,729
See you later!

186
00:10:59,521 --> 00:11:01,357
So, what do you want me to do?

187
00:11:01,565 --> 00:11:03,192
Terai, you teach him.

188
00:11:03,400 --> 00:11:06,820
You're the one in charge of that! I'm going out on patrol too.

189
00:11:07,029 --> 00:11:08,614
Hey!

190
00:11:09,239 --> 00:11:11,408
Sheesh. I have to do everything.

191
00:11:11,617 --> 00:11:13,994
Um... what about me?

192
00:11:14,328 --> 00:11:16,872
Stand outside and help people if they're lost.

193
00:11:17,081 --> 00:11:17,873
Yes, sir!

194
00:11:24,797 --> 00:11:27,591
Excuse me, are you a police officer?

195
00:11:27,800 --> 00:11:29,093
I am.

196
00:11:29,301 --> 00:11:33,180
Oh, good. Would you mind helping me find my way?

197
00:11:33,388 --> 00:11:35,057
Of course.

198
00:11:36,225 --> 00:11:38,519
"KAMEARI PARK POLICE STATION"

199
00:11:38,977 --> 00:11:41,230
Sir, please wake up.

200
00:11:42,481 --> 00:11:45,484
What is it? I was having a nice nap.

201
00:11:45,859 --> 00:11:50,823
A man asked me for directions, but I don't know the area well.

202
00:11:51,031 --> 00:11:51,990
Use that.

203
00:11:52,199 --> 00:11:52,991
Huh?

204
00:11:53,200 --> 00:11:55,536
Tell him to find his own way on that map.

205
00:11:55,744 --> 00:11:59,123
But it's an old man who hasn't lived here in 50 years.

206
00:11:59,331 --> 00:12:02,000
He says he's already totally lost.

207
00:12:02,709 --> 00:12:04,962
All right, fine.

208
00:12:05,754 --> 00:12:07,714
So, where are you wanting to go?

209
00:12:07,923 --> 00:12:09,466
It's a restaurant.

210
00:12:09,675 --> 00:12:10,968
And what's it called?

211
00:12:11,176 --> 00:12:15,389
I'm afraid I've forgotten the name. But I do have a picture.

212
00:12:16,098 --> 00:12:16,974
Huh?

213
00:12:17,599 --> 00:12:18,976
This is it.

214
00:12:19,184 --> 00:12:23,856
That's a pretty bad drawing. Did you draw it?

215
00:12:24,064 --> 00:12:28,485
Yes, when I was a student. That's over 50 years ago now.

216
00:12:28,694 --> 00:12:31,446
Over 50 years ago?

217
00:12:31,655 --> 00:12:33,240
Do you have the address?

218
00:12:33,449 --> 00:12:37,077
I only know it was somewhere in downtown Tokyo.

219
00:12:37,286 --> 00:12:38,996
-That's all? -I'm afraid so.

220
00:12:39,413 --> 00:12:41,874
That's no good. The downtown area is enormous.

221
00:12:42,082 --> 00:12:44,668
We'll never find it. You should give up.

222
00:12:44,877 --> 00:12:49,006
We have to help him. It's my first job as a police officer!

223
00:12:49,214 --> 00:12:50,299
Do as you like.

224
00:12:50,507 --> 00:12:55,679
If you help me find it, I'll give you a reward.

225
00:12:55,888 --> 00:12:58,432
Why didn't you say so sooner?

226
00:12:58,640 --> 00:13:00,726
Let's discuss this in the back room.

227
00:13:01,518 --> 00:13:04,563
Hey, Nakagawa, go get us some coffee and cake.

228
00:13:04,771 --> 00:13:06,982
-What? -Just do it. Quickly!

229
00:13:07,399 --> 00:13:08,734
Yes, sir.

230
00:13:09,193 --> 00:13:16,074
I see. So, you used to go there often when you were attending the art school.

231
00:13:16,325 --> 00:13:17,409
Which art school?

232
00:13:17,618 --> 00:13:23,874
Tokyo University of the Arts. That restaurant was a popular lunch spot.

233
00:13:24,208 --> 00:13:27,085
So it must be near the school, right?

234
00:13:27,294 --> 00:13:31,590
If I remember correctly, it was about 15 minutes away on foot.

235
00:13:31,924 --> 00:13:34,718
Tokyo University of the Arts is in the Ueno district.

236
00:13:38,513 --> 00:13:39,848
You can have mine too.

237
00:13:40,057 --> 00:13:41,683
Thanks!

238
00:13:41,892 --> 00:13:44,770
Let's start by checking the Yanaka and Nezu areas.

239
00:13:44,978 --> 00:13:49,024
Excuse me, will we be able to find it in the next two hours?

240
00:13:49,233 --> 00:13:52,361
It's about 20 or 30 minutes to Ueno by car, so yeah, probably.

241
00:13:52,569 --> 00:13:57,532
I have to catch a plane from Narita to Paris at one o'clock.

242
00:13:58,867 --> 00:14:03,413
Hmm, it's a one-hour train ride to the airport from Ueno.

243
00:14:03,914 --> 00:14:05,707
Nakagawa, hail a taxi.

244
00:14:05,916 --> 00:14:08,835
I'll ring for my car instead.

245
00:14:09,044 --> 00:14:12,631
Yes, it's me. Send the car to the police station right away.

246
00:14:14,174 --> 00:14:17,678
Would you like to have my piece too?

247
00:14:17,886 --> 00:14:19,179
With pleasure!

248
00:14:21,682 --> 00:14:23,058
Ah, it's here.

249
00:14:25,936 --> 00:14:30,148
Whoa, that's a Ferrari F40, isn't it?

250
00:14:30,357 --> 00:14:31,358
As requested, sir.

251
00:14:32,025 --> 00:14:33,569
But isn't this a two-seater?

252
00:14:33,777 --> 00:14:36,613
It had it modified into a four-seater, so it'll be fine.

253
00:14:37,114 --> 00:14:38,532
Get in please, everyone.

254
00:14:43,078 --> 00:14:44,538
Reiko, great timing!

255
00:14:45,080 --> 00:14:47,499
-Ryo-chan? -Watch the station while we help this man.

256
00:14:47,708 --> 00:14:48,500
Huh?

257
00:14:48,709 --> 00:14:49,501
See you later!

258
00:14:50,377 --> 00:14:51,253
Hey!

259
00:14:52,421 --> 00:14:55,465
I've seen that man somewhere before...

260
00:15:00,554 --> 00:15:03,473
Darn it. We don't have time for this.

261
00:15:03,849 --> 00:15:05,934
Hey, Nakagawa, take that turn.

262
00:15:06,143 --> 00:15:09,980
Sir, I can't. It's a one-way street.

263
00:15:10,188 --> 00:15:14,067
You idiot! Don't you want to help this guy?

264
00:15:14,276 --> 00:15:16,987
-It's okay... -Reverse up the street. Then it's fine.

265
00:15:17,195 --> 00:15:18,238
What?

266
00:15:18,947 --> 00:15:22,284
Understood, sir. I'm going in backward.

267
00:15:27,956 --> 00:15:30,375
You didn't need to take things this far.

268
00:15:35,714 --> 00:15:37,257
You maniac!

269
00:15:37,716 --> 00:15:40,010
I can't look.

270
00:15:46,016 --> 00:15:47,559
It's Kankichi Ryotsu!

271
00:15:48,143 --> 00:15:50,062
That's a one-way street!

272
00:15:50,395 --> 00:15:53,899
It must be nice to drive around in a classy sports car like that.

273
00:15:54,107 --> 00:15:57,069
Stop being impressed! We need to arrest him!

274
00:16:01,740 --> 00:16:04,034
Stop that Ferrari!

275
00:16:04,242 --> 00:16:05,952
Sir, what should we do?

276
00:16:06,161 --> 00:16:08,663
This is an emergency. Just ignore them.

277
00:16:08,872 --> 00:16:10,874
Show them what this car can really do!

278
00:16:11,083 --> 00:16:12,042
Roger that!

279
00:16:17,964 --> 00:16:19,800
It's so fast.

280
00:16:20,008 --> 00:16:22,719
Damn that Kankichi Ryotsu!

281
00:16:22,928 --> 00:16:25,597
We'll get him for sure next time!

282
00:16:27,474 --> 00:16:28,850
Okay, take a right there.

283
00:16:30,811 --> 00:16:32,437
Turn left at the end.

284
00:16:32,646 --> 00:16:37,150
How come you know your way around so well?

285
00:16:37,359 --> 00:16:42,114
I played here all the time as a kid. It's like my own backyard.

286
00:16:43,407 --> 00:16:46,201
Even if it's shortcut, the car won't fit.

287
00:16:46,410 --> 00:16:48,704
Idiot! This is your first assignment.

288
00:16:49,121 --> 00:16:55,585
And a real police officer never gives up on an assignment.

289
00:16:56,461 --> 00:17:00,173
Sorry, sir. I was wrong.

290
00:17:00,966 --> 00:17:02,175
Let's go!

291
00:17:05,429 --> 00:17:08,557
It looks even narrower up ahead!

292
00:17:08,932 --> 00:17:12,436
Don't worry. We'll make it through!

293
00:17:12,644 --> 00:17:15,731
I've been down here before, on my bicycle.

294
00:17:16,815 --> 00:17:18,483
See, we made it.

295
00:17:19,067 --> 00:17:20,318
You were right!

296
00:17:25,824 --> 00:17:30,162
Could you stop here for a moment?

297
00:17:31,329 --> 00:17:34,374
I have great memories of this school.

298
00:17:34,916 --> 00:17:36,918
I've lived in Paris for decades now,

299
00:17:37,127 --> 00:17:40,380
but lately I've been thinking about Japan a lot.

300
00:17:40,922 --> 00:17:45,427
I often remember my days as a young art student here.

301
00:17:46,386 --> 00:17:50,640
&lt;i&gt;I used to draw all day,&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;surrounded by good friends.&lt;/i&gt;

302
00:17:51,057 --> 00:17:53,810
&lt;i&gt;Ueno truly was like a forest of art.&lt;/i&gt;

303
00:17:54,186 --> 00:17:59,816
&lt;i&gt;We used to go to galleries every day&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;and talk about art.&lt;/i&gt;

304
00:18:00,275 --> 00:18:03,820
&lt;i&gt;One day, a friend took me to a restaurant&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;and a girl who worked there&lt;/i&gt;

305
00:18:04,029 --> 00:18:06,198
&lt;i&gt;captured my heart.&lt;/i&gt;

306
00:18:06,865 --> 00:18:09,284
&lt;i&gt;She was my first love.&lt;/i&gt;

307
00:18:09,618 --> 00:18:12,537
And that's the restaurant in the picture, isn't it?

308
00:18:12,954 --> 00:18:15,373
How long ago it was...

309
00:18:15,874 --> 00:18:21,755
Just before I was about to graduate, I was laid up with a terrible cold.

310
00:18:22,547 --> 00:18:25,383
&lt;i&gt;She came to the boarding house&lt;/i&gt;

311
00:18:25,926 --> 00:18:28,595
&lt;i&gt;and nursed me back to health.&lt;/i&gt;

312
00:18:33,058 --> 00:18:37,312
&lt;i&gt;After I recovered, I wanted&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;to do something to thank her.&lt;/i&gt;

313
00:18:37,521 --> 00:18:41,817
&lt;i&gt;But I couldn't afford&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;to buy her a nice gift.&lt;/i&gt;

314
00:18:42,317 --> 00:18:46,905
&lt;i&gt;So I painted a portrait of her&lt;/i&gt;

315
00:18:47,572 --> 00:18:50,116
&lt;i&gt;and gave her that instead.&lt;/i&gt;

316
00:18:50,992 --> 00:18:54,913
The smile on her face when she saw it

317
00:18:55,121 --> 00:18:58,542
is deeply engraved in my memory to this day.

318
00:18:59,125 --> 00:19:01,795
And then what happened, sir?

319
00:19:02,003 --> 00:19:06,049
Immediately after graduating, I moved to Paris to continue my studies.

320
00:19:06,258 --> 00:19:08,552
I never even told her how I felt.

321
00:19:09,719 --> 00:19:11,805
But it was long ago now.

322
00:19:12,222 --> 00:19:14,808
Gramps, there's no time for reminiscing!

323
00:19:15,141 --> 00:19:17,394
We barely have an hour left!

324
00:19:18,687 --> 00:19:20,480
Let's find that restaurant.

325
00:19:20,814 --> 00:19:21,606
Yes.

326
00:19:24,568 --> 00:19:28,405
How about here, old man? Does anything look familiar?

327
00:19:31,324 --> 00:19:34,995
I guess a lot must have changed in 50 years.

328
00:19:37,289 --> 00:19:39,207
One hour left.

329
00:19:48,717 --> 00:19:50,302
We're not going to find it.

330
00:19:50,844 --> 00:19:55,557
I suppose I'll just take my memories back to Paris with me.

331
00:19:56,057 --> 00:19:58,560
We still have 10 minutes! I won't give up!

332
00:19:59,185 --> 00:20:00,604
We have to find it.

333
00:20:01,062 --> 00:20:03,773
How can I call myself a cop

334
00:20:03,982 --> 00:20:06,776
if I can't even find a restaurant!

335
00:20:07,319 --> 00:20:09,237
Damn it. Where is it!

336
00:20:13,199 --> 00:20:14,909
I wish we could have reunited you

337
00:20:15,118 --> 00:20:18,872
with the first love you've held in your heart for 50 years.

338
00:20:19,080 --> 00:20:22,584
It's okay. This is what fate has decided.

339
00:20:22,792 --> 00:20:23,585
Hmm?

340
00:20:24,210 --> 00:20:25,545
Those trees...

341
00:20:26,046 --> 00:20:29,174
I found it!

342
00:20:31,384 --> 00:20:35,013
Look, there it is! It's just like in the picture.

343
00:20:35,847 --> 00:20:38,099
It hasn't changed at all.

344
00:20:39,100 --> 00:20:41,394
So, let's go meet your first love.

345
00:20:41,603 --> 00:20:43,605
W-Wait a minute.

346
00:20:43,980 --> 00:20:45,607
What's wrong, old man?

347
00:20:46,024 --> 00:20:49,986
After so many years, she must be married with a family.

348
00:20:50,195 --> 00:20:52,656
It might be wrong to turn up out of the blue.

349
00:20:52,864 --> 00:20:55,283
Don't say that! We went through a lot to find it!

350
00:20:55,492 --> 00:20:56,451
Go inside.

351
00:20:56,660 --> 00:20:57,661
But...

352
00:20:57,869 --> 00:21:00,747
If you don't open the door, I will.

353
00:21:00,955 --> 00:21:01,915
Go on...

354
00:21:06,002 --> 00:21:09,589
Open it. Come on, hurry up!

355
00:21:14,302 --> 00:21:16,805
Mizue-san...

356
00:21:17,305 --> 00:21:20,433
Taki-san. You're Taki-san, aren't you?

357
00:21:21,476 --> 00:21:22,435
Yes.

358
00:21:22,977 --> 00:21:24,562
After so many years!

359
00:21:24,771 --> 00:21:26,106
Yes, too many.

360
00:21:26,314 --> 00:21:30,819
I still have that painting you gave me up on the wall.

361
00:21:31,027 --> 00:21:31,986
Really?

362
00:21:35,740 --> 00:21:39,828
You've taken such good care of it.

363
00:21:40,203 --> 00:21:43,415
Of course. I'll always treasure it.

364
00:21:45,166 --> 00:21:47,544
Thank you so much, Mizue-san.

365
00:21:51,047 --> 00:21:54,509
Sir, look how happy they are.

366
00:21:54,718 --> 00:22:00,598
Yes, it's part of a police officer's job to bring smiles to the public's faces.

367
00:22:01,015 --> 00:22:04,102
This is a wonderful job, isn't it?

368
00:22:04,310 --> 00:22:08,523
Yes, and I wonder how much money the old man'll give me as a reward

369
00:22:08,732 --> 00:22:10,483
S-Sir...

370
00:22:10,984 --> 00:22:14,612
Thanks to you, I was able to make a new precious memory.

371
00:22:14,821 --> 00:22:17,198
Please accept this in return.

372
00:22:17,407 --> 00:22:20,160
Thanks so much.

373
00:22:20,368 --> 00:22:24,372
Well then, I'll be off. Thank you for everything.

374
00:22:24,581 --> 00:22:26,041
Sure, take care.

375
00:22:26,374 --> 00:22:27,876
Goodbye.

376
00:22:29,252 --> 00:22:30,879
Let's get going, shall we?

377
00:22:32,630 --> 00:22:34,924
Another painting?

378
00:22:35,842 --> 00:22:38,428
I couldn't be less happy.

379
00:22:38,887 --> 00:22:41,431
Who'd want a crappy painting like this?

380
00:22:43,516 --> 00:22:45,351
-Hey, kid. -Huh?

381
00:22:45,560 --> 00:22:47,145
You can have this.

382
00:22:47,353 --> 00:22:49,105
Are you sure? It was a gift.

383
00:22:49,314 --> 00:22:51,441
It's fine. Come on, let's go.

384
00:22:54,944 --> 00:22:57,614
Jotaro Taki!

385
00:22:58,823 --> 00:23:01,659
All we got is a few dents in your Ferrari.

386
00:23:01,868 --> 00:23:03,244
Don't worry about it.

387
00:23:03,453 --> 00:23:05,872
I have plenty of other cars back at home.

388
00:23:06,080 --> 00:23:08,166
You're that rich, huh?

389
00:23:08,500 --> 00:23:12,629
I suppose so. Our assets add up to about 400 billion yen.

390
00:23:12,837 --> 00:23:14,631
400 billion?

391
00:23:14,839 --> 00:23:17,133
Nakagawa-kun, let's be buddies!

392
00:23:17,342 --> 00:23:19,719
Ryo-chan, this is serious.

393
00:23:19,928 --> 00:23:22,138
You know that old man you had in the Ferrari?

394
00:23:22,347 --> 00:23:24,182
That shabby old guy?

395
00:23:24,390 --> 00:23:25,350
Don't be silly.

396
00:23:25,558 --> 00:23:28,436
He's a world-famous painter. Look.

397
00:23:29,354 --> 00:23:31,564
That certainly does look like him.

398
00:23:32,023 --> 00:23:33,942
He's really that famous, huh?

399
00:23:34,150 --> 00:23:38,071
Each of his paintings sell for at least 100 million yen.

400
00:23:38,279 --> 00:23:40,073
A 100 million!

401
00:23:40,406 --> 00:23:42,325
Oh no!

402
00:23:43,618 --> 00:23:45,495
Damn it, Ryotsu!

403
00:23:45,703 --> 00:23:48,498
You can shout at me as much as you want later!

404
00:23:48,706 --> 00:23:52,418
My 100 million yen!

405
00:23:53,711 --> 00:23:56,965
TODAY'S DAMAGE REPORT

406
00:23:57,173 --> 00:23:59,717
1 CAR, 1 MOTORBIKE, SEVERAL TRASHCANS

407
00:23:59,926 --> 00:24:02,470
LOSS OF 100 MILLION YEN

408
00:24:05,014 --> 00:24:07,517
&lt;i&gt;I've had a brilliant idea!&lt;/i&gt;

409
00:24:07,725 --> 00:24:09,477
&lt;i&gt;We'll sell ramen from the air.&lt;/i&gt;

410
00:24:09,936 --> 00:24:11,855
&lt;i&gt;It's a store that flies!&lt;/i&gt;

411
00:24:12,063 --> 00:24:14,858
&lt;i&gt;Nobody else could come up&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;with a great idea like this.&lt;/i&gt;

412
00:24:15,316 --> 00:24:17,402
&lt;i&gt;I must be a genius!&lt;/i&gt;

413
00:24:17,986 --> 00:24:22,991
NEXT EPISODE FOOD CART BUSINESS FLYING HIGH!

414
00:24:32,917 --> 00:24:37,213
&lt;i&gt;Let's keep smiling always&lt;/i&gt;

415
00:24:37,839 --> 00:24:41,467
&lt;i&gt;Even when things go wrong&lt;/i&gt;

416
00:24:41,676 --> 00:24:45,930
&lt;i&gt;Keep a pretty smile on your face&lt;/i&gt;

417
00:24:46,556 --> 00:24:51,019
&lt;i&gt;And go out as if nothing happened&lt;/i&gt;

418
00:24:51,561 --> 00:24:55,064
&lt;i&gt;Hey, show me your smile&lt;/i&gt;

419
00:24:55,273 --> 00:24:59,277
&lt;i&gt;You did nothing wrong&lt;/i&gt;

420
00:25:00,236 --> 00:25:03,740
&lt;i&gt;Hey, show me your smile&lt;/i&gt;

421
00:25:03,948 --> 00:25:07,410
&lt;i&gt;Just like you did before, yeah&lt;/i&gt;

422
00:25:07,911 --> 00:25:12,081
&lt;i&gt;I want you to smile always&lt;/i&gt;

423
00:25:12,790 --> 00:25:17,212
&lt;i&gt;A woman with a frown isn't pretty&lt;/i&gt;

424
00:25:17,712 --> 00:25:23,259
&lt;i&gt;So you should smile as soon as you can&lt;/i&gt;

425
00:25:24,052 --> 00:25:27,013
&lt;i&gt;It's the grown-up thing to do&lt;/i&gt;

426
00:25:39,150 --> 00:25:43,863
KOCHIKAME SEE YOU NEXT TIME!
